      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree. Some worlds and avatars are more frequented and favored, but it feels strange to keep loading, for instance, your home world, your three favorite avatars, your close-knit friendship group, and a few game worlds you like to play every day. VR Chat's cache system seems to behave quite strangely. While the cache holds 20 GB of data, I'm still required to download the people and places I go that never change.\nThe option to specify worlds, avatars, and friends in download will make it much faster for those items to appear, alleviate strain on metered network connections, and VRC servers. Any suggestions that can function better automatically can help, but I think users definitely need to specify what they want. Like Spotify.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-07-28T12:42:06.847Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Say you go to a 500 MB event world every two weeks. Even with a large VRChat cache size, you'd most likely end up having to always redownload the same world. It would be useful to pin select worlds and/or avatars to always have cached.",
